  "raw": {
    "https://swosu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/752?c=swosu": {
      "title": "Instructor of English",
      "description": "Instructor of English | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Instructor of English United States | req752 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Instructor of English Job Title Instructor of English Department Language & Literature Posting Number req752 Description of Job Duties Job Summary: The Department of Language and Literature at Southwestern Oklahoma State University (SWOSU) invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, Instructor of English at the Weatherford location. This position is renewable annually in accordance with the university’s faculty evaluation provisions. Description of Job Duties: The Department of Language and Literature seeks qualified individuals to serve as a full-time Instructor of English. Teaching responsibilities include English Composition I, English Composition II, and associated support courses. Teaching assignments will be primarily in-person with possible online, blended, or synchronous Zoom courses depending on departmental needs. The instructor's salary is $49,986. The successful candidate will be responsible for: Teaching assignments mentioned above Maintaining weekly office hours appropriate to course load Expectations are to maintain a Canvas site for each course and gain a working knowledge of the Colleague system Participating in early grade alert systems and assessing student outcomes Participating in departmental assessment Advising students and supporting student activities Continuing professional development Work Setting & Expectations: Reports to the Chair of the Language and Literature Department. Completion of safety and job-related training as required. Salary determined according to SWOSU’s wage structure. Responsible for following safety procedures and maintaining a safe work environment. Exempt position. Employment at will. Application: The full application requires the following documents and will need to be submitted through the official SWOSU employment portal: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (preferred) or Resumé Teaching Philosophy Statement Transcripts (unofficial) Anticipated start date: Fall 2027 About SWOSU: With campuses in Weatherford, Yukon, and Sayre, as well as a range of online degree programs, Southwestern Oklahoma State University is recognized as a leading regional university. Discover what makes SWOSU and Weatherford a great place to learn, work, and thrive. Education and Experience Education and Experience: A graduate degree in English, Writing Studies, English Education, or a related field is required. A degree in rhetoric and composition studies is preferred. Prior teaching experience at the collegiate level is preferred. Technological competence and experience in the LMS Canvas is preferred. Anticipated Start Date 8/11/2027 Location Weatherford Employment Type Exempt Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://swosu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/747?c=swosu": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of History/Coordinator of History Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of History/Coordinator of History Education | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor of History/Coordinator of History Education United States | req747 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/16/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of History/Coordinator of History Education Job Title Assistant Professor of History/Coordinator of History Education Department Social Sciences Posting Number req747 Description of Job Duties Job Summary: The Department of Social Sciences at Southwestern Oklahoma State University (SWOSU) invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Early World History and Coordinator of the History Education Program. Description of Job Duties: The successful candidate will serve as both an Early World History professor and the Program Coordinator for the nationally accredited History Education program, which includes supervising the student teaching field experiences, teaching the required Methods course for Social Studies secondary education, and maintaining documentation and data for the purposes of preserving the program’s accreditation.  The candidate will also advise History Education majors, ensuring that teacher candidates have fulfilled the minimum hours required for field experiences. Finally, the successful candidate will teach General Education courses both online and in-person in subjects such as Early World History and World Cultural Geography, in addition to upper-division courses in their area of expertise. The successful candidate will be responsible for: Completing systematic program reviews to ensure content alignment with the Council for Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP) and national or state approved standards. Evaluate assessments to ensure content aligns with teacher competencies and state and national standards, review and adjust processes for assessment redevelopment, and track passing rates on subject-area tests to analyze and target potential obstacles to teacher certification. Serve on the Teacher Education Council (TEC) and coordinate History Education program accreditation processes, which includes attending TEC meetings. Attending NCSS annual training sessions and overseeing the implementation of any SPA standard changes to the History Education program. Maintaining weekly office hours appropriate to course load Participating in early grade alert systems and assessing student outcomes Advising students and supporting student activities Continuing professional development Work Setting & Expectations Reports to the Chair of the Social Sciences Department. Completion of safety and job-related training as required. Salary determined according to SWOSU’s wage structure. Responsible for following safety procedures and maintaining a safe work environment. Full-time, 9-month, exempt position. Employment at will. Application submission deadline: November 6, 2026 Education and Experience Education and Experience Ph.D. in History preferred. Must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Familiarity with InTASC Core Teaching Standards, CAEP accreditation standards, and C3 Framework is preferred. Prior teaching experience at the secondary and collegiate level is preferred. Technological competence and experience in the LMS Canvas is preferred. Expectations are to maintain a Canvas site for each course and gain a working knowledge of the Colleague system. Candidates must include a statement on teaching philosophy. Anticipated Start Date 8/11/2027 Location Weatherford Employment Type Exempt Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://swosu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/746?c=swosu": {
      "title": "Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) Instructor",
      "description": "Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) Instructor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) Instructor United States | req746 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/16/2026 Back to Search Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) Instructor Job Title Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) Instructor Department Allied Health Sciences Posting Number req746 Description of Job Duties Job Summary: The Department of Allied Health Sciences seeks a qualified individual to serve as a temporary MLT Instructor for the Spring 2027 semester. Under minimal supervision, provides instruction, participates in student management, and functions as a member of the Allied Health Sciences faculty. Job performance will be periodically evaluated by the AHS Coordinator of Applied Programs, the Allied Health Sciences Department Chair, and the Dean of the College of Nursing and Health Professions in accordance with the provisions of the University’s policies on evaluations of faculty. Description of Job Duties: Under direction of the MLT Program Director, develop a learning environment that offers opportunities for active participation in the learning process by providing traditional instruction in the Medical Laboratory Technician Program courses and labs. Ability to plan and prepare course and lab content and curriculum, using effective methodologies of instruction for the enhancement of learning. Initiate and maintain effective communication and collaboration with the MLT Program Director and associated faculty. Maintain expertise in field of study and teaching pedagogy by attending seminars, workshops, and classes for self-improvement and/or professional enhancement. Maintain active participation in professional organizations and/or service organizations as appropriate. Participate in recruitment, advisement, and enrollment management for medical laboratory technician students. Support student activities, including course and career guidance and mentoring students. Other tasks as assigned by the MLT Program Director, AHS Coordinator of Applied Programs, or AHS Department Chair. Work Setting: Expectation of on-campus presence with attendance and punctuality Promote personal safety, safety procedures, and a safe work environment Employment at will Full-time status, temporary Exempt About SWOSU: With locations in Weatherford, Yukon, Sayre, and online degree programs, SWOSU is one of the leading regional universities in the country. See what makes SWOSU and Weatherford so great! Education and Experience Education & Experience: Associate’s Degree is required Bachelor of Science in an appropriate field (Medical Technology, Biology, Chemistry or Allied Health) is preferred Master’s degree is preferred Applicant must be certified as a Medical Laboratory Technician/Medical Laboratory Scientist Clinical laboratory experience is required Previous teaching experience preferred Anticipated Start Date 1/11/2027 Location Weatherford Employment Type Exempt Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://swosu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/742?c=swosu": {
      "title": "Nursing Instructor",
      "description": "Nursing Instructor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Nursing Instructor United States | req742 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/3/2026 Back to Search Nursing Instructor Job Title Nursing Instructor Department Nursing Posting Number req742 Description of Job Duties Job Summary The SWOSU Nursing Department seeks qualified applicants for a full-time, in-person Nursing Instructor. This position is responsible for delivering high-quality instruction in classroom, laboratory, simulation, and clinical settings. Responsibilities include planning and teaching curriculum aligned with program outcomes, maintaining expertise in nursing practice and education, advising pre-nursing students, evaluating student performance, and ensuring compliance with accreditation and licensure standards. Description of Job Responsibilities: Create and maintain a caring, engaging, and positive learning environment. Plan and deliver course content and assessments aligned with current curriculum and program outcomes. The Department Chair makes teaching assignments. Teach according to approved syllabi and provide timely updates, grading, and communication regarding course expectations and student progress. Coordinate assigned classroom, laboratory, simulation, and clinical learning experiences. Use instructional technologies and consider varied learning styles to support student success. Maintain accurate scholastic records, including attendance and grade documentation. Submit course syllabi each term to the Program Coordinator. Provide academic and career guidance, mentoring, and referrals to campus resources. Maintain posted office hours and support student retention and success. Maintain nursing and teaching expertise and participate in professional organizations. Participate in curriculum evaluation and program review; make recommendations for improvement. Conduct formative and summative assessments, including exams, quizzes, evaluations, and other measures. Recommend textbooks, instructional materials, technologies, and lab resources. Ensure hybrid/online courses meet the same rigor, quality, and privacy standards as traditional courses. Clinical supervision: Integrate theory with supervised clinical performance in assigned settings. Orient students and communicate clinical objectives to students and adjunct clinical faculty. Guide, supervise, and evaluate students in patient care and skills performance. Mentor and support adjunct clinical faculty. Travel to and from clinical sites as required. Participate in departmental and university committees as assigned. Ensure compliance with accreditation and nursing regulatory board requirements. Perform other duties as assigned by program leadership, department chair, or university administration. Work Setting & Expectations Reports to the Traditional BSN Program Coordinator. Completion of safety and job-related training as required. Salary determined according to SWOSU’s wage structure. Responsible for following safety procedures and maintaining a safe work environment. Full-time, 9-month, exempt position. Employment at will. About SWOSU With campuses in Weatherford, Yukon, and Sayre, as well as a range of online degree programs, Southwestern Oklahoma State University is recognized as a leading regional university. Discover what makes SWOSU and Weatherford a great place to learn, work, and thrive. Education and Experience Education & Licensure Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) required. Minimum two years of clinical nursing experience required. Community nursing experience preferred. Current, unencumbered Oklahoma RN license. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Demonstrate leadership, professionalism, and collegiality. Strong organizational and time-management skills; ability to meet deadlines. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Proficiency with Microsoft Office (Word, Outlook, PowerPoint) and learning management system (Canvas). Effective written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to present information to small and large groups. Ability to manage stress, maintain emotional stability, and support students effectively. Ability to sit/stand for extended periods, bend, kneel, reach, climb steps, and lift up to 50 lbs. Basic mathematical competency (rates, fractions, etc.). Anticipated Start Date 1/7/2027 Location Weatherford Employment Type Exempt Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://swosu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/719?c=swosu": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor of Biology United States | req719 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/1/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Biology Job Title Assistant Professor of Biology Department Biological Sciences Posting Number req719 Description of Job Duties Description of Job Duties: The Department of Biological and Biomedical Sciences at SWOSU seeks a qualified individual to serve as an Assistant Professor of Biology with an emphasis in Cell Biology. Primary teaching responsibilities include courses in Cell Biology, participation in one or more core Biology courses, and teaching within the candidate’s area of expertise. Additional responsibilities may include supporting pre-professional courses (Molecular Biology, Cancer Biology, and Microbiology), as well as general education biology (Principles of Biology, Biological Concepts, and Current Issues in Biology). The candidate is expected to engage students in undergraduate research and work with colleagues to integrate research into the biology curriculum. Startup funds and research space are available. The candidate is expected to participate in department and university service. Our department values collegiality as we strive to provide an excellent and welcoming learning environment for students. Additional information about the department can be found at: https://www.swosu.edu/academics/degrees/biological-sciences-bs.php . The successful candidate will be responsible for: Teaching assignments referenced above Maintaining weekly office hours appropriate to course load Participating in early grade alert systems and assessing student outcomes Departmental assessment Student advisement and support of student activities Continuing professional development Scholarly activity in related area Anticipated Start Date: January 2027 Deadline Date: Review of applications will begin June 1 and continue until the position is filled Application Procedure Submit cover letter referencing Position, vita including links to publications, unofficial transcripts, teaching philosophy, research plan and the names and contact information of three references to the online portal. For more information visit www.swosu.edu . Education and Experience Education and Experience A Ph.D. in the Biological Sciences is required, with graduate coursework and a demonstrated research emphasis in cell biology. Post-doctoral research and/or teaching experience are preferred. Technological competence and experience in Canvas is preferred. Expectations are to maintain a Canvas site for each course and gain a working knowledge of the Colleague system. Anticipated Start Date 1/8/2027 Location Weatherford Employment Type Exempt Apply Now Share Save Job"
    }
